This error-robustness of VQE-E can be understood as follow. The impact of local
errors which occur individually for distinct measurement setups of non-commuting
observables, amplifies the error of expectation value of the Hamiltonian since all
the expectations of Pauli strings would be appended together to obtain Hamiltonian
expectation value.
In contrast, as demonstrated in the Heisenberg model where all
terms are measured in a single Bell measurement setup, all terms are affected by
errors that occurred in the same system, and the heuristic optimization process guides


